# Profile: oauth-supabase
# The OAuth authorization server with Supabase as the consent-step identity provider, proven END TO END
# against a FAKE Supabase auth service: the sidecar nsc-acc-supabase serves the project's JWKS (the public
# half of a key the harness generates per run); the harness signs the session token itself and posts it to
# /oauth/supabase/callback the way the sign-in finisher page does. Everything on the stack side (JWKS fetch,
# signature/audience/expiry checks, allowlist, identity resolution, link page, authorization code, PKCE token
# exchange) is the real code; only the identity provider is faked. Nothing here can reach a real Supabase.
# requires: compose
# sidecars: nsc-acc-supabase
# The gate needs nothing beyond the compose stack and the python:3.12-alpine image (docker pull it once).
# The port is the gate's private API port (18199); the issuer URL must equal the URL the run targets
# (the scenarios assert it). If the gate uses another port, change this one line for the run.
NEURALSCAPE_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18199
AUTH_PROVIDER=supabase
# The sidecar's address on the stack's compose network (sidecar.PORT); the scenarios assert it.
SUPABASE_URL=http://nsc-acc-supabase:8080
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<generate:hex32>
# Allowlist: one domain (the scenarios' people) and one exact address on another domain (the guest path).
AUTH_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=acceptance-placeholder.example
AUTH_EMAIL_ALLOWLIST=acc-guest@acceptance-guest.example
# One person with an admin-assigned id (email:user_id); everyone else gets the email slug.
AUTH_IDENTITY_MAP=acc-mapped@acceptance-placeholder.example:acc-supabase-mapped
